   "additionalProperties": false,
   "answer": "Evidence saturation is the collapse of marginal yield of new independent mechanisms per additional diverse query: after MIN_QUERIES=6 and at least one independent mechanism found, the last STREAK_K=3 queries each add YIELD_FLOOR=0 new mechanisms AND those three queries use three distinct query families. Independence is mechanism_id, not source_id string equality, so mirrored copies of one paper cannot pad a count. Search fatigue is the same yield collapse produced by repeating one query family; that path sets evidence_saturation=false and reason=search_fatigue, so it does not satisfy the saturation arm. The both-states control is: FIRE on saturated-12 (12/12 mechanisms found, then three diverse zero-yield queries, time_minutes=40<180, which_arm=evidence_saturation) and SILENT on unsaturated-12 (still yielding, time_minutes=40, which_arm=none). The OR with time_minutes>=180 is a distinct arm: time-arm-180 uses the unsaturated log at t=180, fires with which_arm=time_minutes and saturation_arm=false, so a never-firing detector cannot hide behind the disjunction.",
